From 0385233a5168870cdf8191dc3488f26574eedf94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bertholomus <311723197+bertholomus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:49:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] engine: borrow the GB10 display carveout for the weight image
 (GR8_ATTIC_SOCK)

A headless GB10 never uses the ~2 GiB the driver reserves for a display. A carveout lender
(spark-attic's atticd, which speaks KindlingAI's dispramd socket protocol) lends it as 2 MiB
slices over a Unix socket. With GR8_ATTIC_SOCK and GR8_ATTIC_KEY_FILE set, each rank asks its
own box's lender for one slice that spans the weight image's G.embed (the full vocabulary in
BF16, 1,815 MiB a rank, of which a step reads only its tokens' rows), imports the descriptor
and maps the image around it through the CUDA VMM API (vmm.h alloc_around). The image then
takes that much less ordinary memory, so a larger --cap fits. Same bytes at the same offsets;
the KV pool stays in ordinary memory.

Unset, nothing runs and nothing is printed. Fail open: no daemon, a refusal, a short lend, a
key that cannot be sent, or a slice the driver will not map builds the image as GR8_IMG_VMM
says, after one line saying why.

- engine/attic_proto.h, engine/attic.h: the protocol and the client.
- engine/vmm.h: alloc_around maps the image around the slice in 1 GiB pieces. Each physical
  allocation costs the kernel ~25 KB of slab, so 2 MiB pieces cost ~1 GiB for an 81 GB image
  (16 GiB test on a GB10: slab +0.004 GiB instead of +0.24).
- engine/runtime/packfind.h: g6m4 and m4sim declare a global namespace bind, so the socket
  headers come in with bind renamed (as runtime/s2/posix_socket.h does).
- engine/tests/attic_test.cpp (host, in scripts/host_tests.sh): request bytes, the key rule,
  replies, and a fake lender over a real socket. engine/tests/vmm_around_test.cu (GB10).
- knobs/runtime.yaml: GR8_ATTIC_SOCK, GR8_ATTIC_KEY_FILE; generated files from knobs -- gen.
